{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Tide Level Prediction Pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook starts the full workflow for Sandy Hook tide forecasting:\n",
        "- data loading and preprocessing\n",
        "- feature engineering for time series ML\n",
        "- light EDA and time series checks\n",
        "- scaling-ready train/validation/test datasets\n",
        "- regression target (`Water_Level`) and severity classification target\n",
        "\n",
        "We will keep all engineered features **past-safe**, so the same setup can later support classical ML models, LSTM models, and a web app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid')\n",
        "sns.set_palette('deep')\n",
        "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', 100)\n",
        "\n",
        "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
        "DATA_PATH = Path('sandy_hook_2024_multivariate.csv')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Load Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df_raw = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
        "print(df_raw.shape)\n",
        "df_raw.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Basic Checks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print('Columns:', list(df_raw.columns))\n",
        "print('\\nDtypes before preprocessing:')\n",
        "print(df_raw.dtypes)\n",
        "print('\\nMissing values:')\n",
        "print(df_raw.isna().sum())\n",
        "print('\\nDuplicate rows:', df_raw.duplicated().sum())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "Main steps:\n",
        "- parse timestamp\n",
        "- sort by time\n",
        "- enforce hourly frequency\n",
        "- identify missing timestamps\n",
        "- interpolate weather/ocean measurements carefully for modeling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = df_raw.copy()\n",
        "df['Date Time'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date Time'])\n",
        "df = df.sort_values('Date Time').drop_duplicates(subset='Date Time').set_index('Date Time')\n",
        "\n",
        "full_index = pd.date_range(df.index.min(), df.index.max(), freq='H')\n",
        "missing_timestamps = full_index.difference(df.index)\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Original rows:', len(df))\n",
        "print('Expected hourly rows:', len(full_index))\n",
        "print('Missing timestamps count:', len(missing_timestamps))\n",
        "print('\\nFirst missing timestamps:')\n",
        "print(missing_timestamps[:10])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = df.reindex(full_index)\n",
        "df.index.name = 'Date Time'\n",
        "\n",
        "numeric_cols = ['Water_Level', 'Wind_Speed', 'Pressure', 'Air_Temp', 'Water_Temp']\n",
        "df[numeric_cols] = df[numeric_cols].interpolate(method='time').ffill().bfill()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(df.shape)\n",
        "print('\\nMissing values after hourly reindex + interpolation:')\n",
        "print(df.isna().sum())\n",
        "df.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Light EDA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "display(df.describe().T)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 2, figsize=(15, 10))\n",
        "axes = axes.flatten()\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, col in enumerate(numeric_cols):\n",
        "    sns.histplot(df[col], kde=True, ax=axes[i])\n",
        "    axes[i].set_title(f'{col} distribution')\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[-1].axis('off')\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(numeric_cols), 1, figsize=(16, 12), sharex=True)\n",
        "for ax, col in zip(axes, numeric_cols):\n",
        "    ax.plot(df.index, df[col], linewidth=0.8)\n",
        "    ax.set_title(col)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "sns.heatmap(df[numeric_cols].corr(), annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', fmt='.2f')\n",
        "plt.title('Correlation Matrix')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Time Series View\n",
        "\n",
        "This is intentionally light. The goal is to understand seasonality and short-term temporal behavior before training models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "daily_tide = df['Water_Level'].resample('D').mean()\n",
        "weekly_tide = df['Water_Level'].resample('W').mean()\n",
        "monthly_tide = df['Water_Level'].resample('M').mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(16, 10), sharex=False)\n",
        "daily_tide.plot(ax=axes[0], title='Daily Mean Water Level')\n",
        "weekly_tide.plot(ax=axes[1], title='Weekly Mean Water Level')\n",
        "monthly_tide.plot(ax=axes[2], title='Monthly Mean Water Level')\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "lags = [1, 2, 3, 6, 12, 24]\n",
        "autocorr_values = {f'lag_{lag}': df['Water_Level'].autocorr(lag=lag) for lag in lags}\n",
        "pd.Series(autocorr_values, name='water_level_autocorr')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Feature Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "Good tide prediction features usually include:\n",
        "- calendar time features\n",
        "- cyclical encodings for hour/day/month\n",
        "- lag features from recent water level and meteorology\n",
        "- rolling statistics for short-term history\n",
        "- rate-of-change features\n",
        "\n",
        "Important rule for deployment: use only values available up to the prediction timestamp."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "feature_df = df.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calendar features\n",
        "feature_df['hour'] = feature_df.index.hour\n",
        "feature_df['day_of_week'] = feature_df.index.dayofweek\n",
        "feature_df['day_of_month'] = feature_df.index.day\n",
        "feature_df['month'] = feature_df.index.month\n",
        "feature_df['day_of_year'] = feature_df.index.dayofyear\n",
        "feature_df['is_weekend'] = (feature_df['day_of_week'] >= 5).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cyclical encodings\n",
        "feature_df['hour_sin'] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * feature_df['hour'] / 24)\n",
        "feature_df['hour_cos'] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * feature_df['hour'] / 24)\n",
        "feature_df['dayofyear_sin'] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * feature_df['day_of_year'] / 365.25)\n",
        "feature_df['dayofyear_cos'] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * feature_df['day_of_year'] / 365.25)\n",
        "feature_df['month_sin'] = np.sin(2 * np.pi * feature_df['month'] / 12)\n",
        "feature_df['month_cos'] = np.cos(2 * np.pi * feature_df['month'] / 12)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Lag features\n",
        "lag_hours = [1, 2, 3, 6, 12, 24]\n",
        "for lag in lag_hours:\n",
        "    feature_df[f'water_level_lag_{lag}'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].shift(lag)\n",
        "    feature_df[f'wind_speed_lag_{lag}'] = feature_df['Wind_Speed'].shift(lag)\n",
        "    feature_df[f'pressure_lag_{lag}'] = feature_df['Pressure'].shift(lag)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Rolling features\n",
        "rolling_windows = [3, 6, 12, 24]\n",
        "for window in rolling_windows:\n",
        "    feature_df[f'water_level_roll_mean_{window}'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].shift(1).rolling(window).mean()\n",
        "    feature_df[f'water_level_roll_std_{window}'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].shift(1).rolling(window).std()\n",
        "    feature_df[f'wind_speed_roll_mean_{window}'] = feature_df['Wind_Speed'].shift(1).rolling(window).mean()\n",
        "    feature_df[f'pressure_roll_mean_{window}'] = feature_df['Pressure'].shift(1).rolling(window).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Change features\n",
        "feature_df['water_level_diff_1'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].diff(1)\n",
        "feature_df['water_level_diff_3'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].diff(3)\n",
        "feature_df['pressure_diff_1'] = feature_df['Pressure'].diff(1)\n",
        "feature_df['wind_speed_diff_1'] = feature_df['Wind_Speed'].diff(1)\n",
        "feature_df['air_water_temp_gap'] = feature_df['Air_Temp'] - feature_df['Water_Temp']\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_df.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Create Regression and Severity Targets\n",
        "\n",
        "For severity classification, we need thresholds. Start with domain-based thresholds and adjust later using local tide-risk understanding.\n",
        "\n",
        "Current example:\n",
        "- `safe`: water level < 0.5\n",
        "- `medium`: 0.5 <= water level < 1.0\n",
        "- `severe`: water level >= 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "SAFE_THRESHOLD = 0.5\n",
        "SEVERE_THRESHOLD = 1.0\n",
        "\n",
        "def classify_severity(water_level, safe_threshold=SAFE_THRESHOLD, severe_threshold=SEVERE_THRESHOLD):\n",
        "    if water_level < safe_threshold:\n",
        "        return 'safe'\n",
        "    if water_level < severe_threshold:\n",
        "        return 'medium'\n",
        "    return 'severe'\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_df['severity_class'] = feature_df['Water_Level'].apply(classify_severity)\n",
        "feature_df['severity_code'] = feature_df['severity_class'].map({'safe': 0, 'medium': 1, 'severe': 2})\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_df[['Water_Level', 'severity_class', 'severity_code']].head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "feature_df['severity_class'].value_counts().sort_index().plot(kind='bar', figsize=(7, 4), title='Severity Class Distribution')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Count')\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_df['severity_class'].value_counts(normalize=True).sort_index()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Prepare Model Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "We drop rows with lag/rolling NaNs created by feature engineering. Then we use a **time-based split** instead of random shuffling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model_df = feature_df.dropna().copy()\n",
        "print(model_df.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "target_reg = 'Water_Level'\n",
        "target_cls = 'severity_code'\n",
        "drop_cols = ['severity_class', 'severity_code']\n",
        "feature_cols = [col for col in model_df.columns if col not in drop_cols]\n",
        "\n",
        "X = model_df[feature_cols]\n",
        "y_reg = model_df[target_reg]\n",
        "y_cls = model_df[target_cls]\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Feature count:', len(feature_cols))\n",
        "print('First 15 features:')\n",
        "print(feature_cols[:15])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "n = len(model_df)\n",
        "train_end = int(n * 0.7)\n",
        "val_end = int(n * 0.85)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = X.iloc[:train_end].copy()\n",
        "X_val = X.iloc[train_end:val_end].copy()\n",
        "X_test = X.iloc[val_end:].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "y_train_reg = y_reg.iloc[:train_end].copy()\n",
        "y_val_reg = y_reg.iloc[train_end:val_end].copy()\n",
        "y_test_reg = y_reg.iloc[val_end:].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "y_train_cls = y_cls.iloc[:train_end].copy()\n",
        "y_val_cls = y_cls.iloc[train_end:val_end].copy()\n",
        "y_test_cls = y_cls.iloc[val_end:].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Train:', X_train.shape, y_train_reg.shape, y_train_cls.shape)\n",
        "print('Validation:', X_val.shape, y_val_reg.shape, y_val_cls.shape)\n",
        "print('Test:', X_test.shape, y_test_reg.shape, y_test_cls.shape)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Scaling\n",
        "\n",
        "Scale using only the training split to avoid leakage. Save the scaler later with the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_scaled = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    scaler.fit_transform(X_train),\n",
        "    index=X_train.index,\n",
        "    columns=X_train.columns\n",
        ")\n",
        "X_val_scaled = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    scaler.transform(X_val),\n",
        "    index=X_val.index,\n",
        "    columns=X_val.columns\n",
        ")\n",
        "X_test_scaled = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    scaler.transform(X_test),\n",
        "    index=X_test.index,\n",
        "    columns=X_test.columns\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(X_train_scaled.head())\n",
        "print('Scaled train mean (approx):', round(float(X_train_scaled.mean().mean()), 4))\n",
        "print('Scaled train std (approx):', round(float(X_train_scaled.std().mean()), 4))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 10. Recommended Next Modeling Steps\n",
        "\n",
        "Classical regression models to try:\n",
        "- Linear Regression\n",
        "- Ridge / Lasso\n",
        "- Random Forest Regressor\n",
        "- Gradient Boosting / XGBoost / LightGBM\n",
        "\n",
        "Severity classification models to try:\n",
        "- Logistic Regression\n",
        "- Random Forest Classifier\n",
        "- XGBoost / LightGBM classifier\n",
        "\n",
        "Deep learning option:\n",
        "- LSTM or GRU with sequence windows such as past 24 or 48 hours\n",
        "\n",
        "Important note:\n",
        "If you train an LSTM later, do not use manually created lag columns in the same way. Instead, create sequence tensors from recent hourly observations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 11. Features Needed Later for Web App\n",
        "\n",
        "For deployment, the app should provide these raw inputs for the latest timestamp:\n",
        "- forecast/current wind speed\n",
        "- pressure\n",
        "- air temperature\n",
        "- water temperature if available\n",
        "- timestamp\n",
        "\n",
        "The backend can then compute:\n",
        "- calendar and cyclical features\n",
        "- recent lag values from stored history\n",
        "- rolling averages and short-term changes\n",
        "\n",
        "If the API cannot provide `Water_Temp`, we can train an alternate model without it."
      ]
    }
  ],
